# Chapter 1, Lust. One cue per encounter.
# The soul only says what the player picks; it has no lines of its own.

~ waking
Velvet: [i](somewhere in the dark, sniffing)[/i] Mm. A new one. Still warm.
Velvet: Don't go looking for your life. It stayed up there. Everybody keeps one thing on the way down.
Velvet: Your name. Say it, before that goes too.
=> END

~ name_empty
Velvet: Nothing? Everybody keeps the name, sinner. Try again.
=> END

~ named
Velvet: {{GameState.player_name}}. [i](tasting it)[/i] That's all you brought? Good. Light ones are easier to carry.
=> END

~ velvet
Velvet: [i](sniffing the air)[/i] Fresh. You still smell of up there.
Velvet: [i](sniffing at the cross in your hand)[/i] And a cross. My favorite kind. I can smell the wanting on it.
Velvet: I'm Velvet. I keep the door.
=> velvet_questions

~ velvet_questions
if locals.asked_who and locals.asked_what_happened and locals.asked_dead and locals.asked_where
	=> velvet_argument
- Who are you? [if not locals.asked_who /]
	$> locals.asked_who = true
	Velvet: I meet the new ones. I sniff out what they want, and walk them to her.
	Velvet: I belong to Asmodeus. She keeps the ones who give in, and I get the leftovers.
	=> velvet_questions
- What happened to me? [if not locals.asked_what_happened /]
	$> locals.asked_what_happened = true
	Velvet: You died. How, I couldn't say. You didn't bring that with you.
	Velvet: You kept your name. The rest stayed up there. Don't ask me to fetch it.
	=> velvet_questions
- Am I dead? [if not locals.asked_dead /]
	$> locals.asked_dead = true
	Velvet: Sinner, you're the deadest thing I've sniffed all week. And I've sniffed plenty.
	=> velvet_questions
- Where am I? [if not locals.asked_where /]
	$> locals.asked_where = true
	Velvet: [i](stretching, like a dog after a long nap)[/i] Hell. First floor: Lust. Here you get what you want. Again and again.
	=> velvet_questions
- Just tell me how to get out.
	=> velvet_argument

~ velvet_argument
Velvet: Out? [i](laughing)[/i] On your first day? Why should you get out?
- I don't belong here. I was a good person.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"arrogant")
	Velvet: [i](sniffing you, slowly)[/i] Everybody here was a good person. Ask around.
	Velvet: They get quieter on the way up.
- Maybe I do belong here. I don't know.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"humble")
	Velvet: [i](licking her chops)[/i] Honest. Honest ones go bad slower. Not much slower.
- I don't have to tell you anything.
	Velvet: [i](grinning)[/i] No. You'll tell her.
Velvet: Asmodeus decides who leaves. She's at the top of the floor.
Velvet: [i](her tail swaying)[/i] Climb. I'll tell her you're coming.
=> END

~ velvet_again
Velvet: Still here? Asmodeus decides who leaves. Up you go.
=> END

~ velvet_advance
Velvet: [i](from inside the fog)[/i] Shh. Nobody up there is watching anymore. Let your body decide, for once.
- Get away from me.
	Velvet: Your mouth says go. The rest of you isn't so sure.
- …and lead us not into temptation…
	$> GameState.mark_event(&"prayed")
	Velvet: [i](backing off a step)[/i] Ugh. Nobody prays on the first floor. It ruins the mood.
- (Say nothing.)
	Velvet: [i](purring)[/i] Good. Words only get in the way.
=> END

~ velvet_burned
Velvet: Ow! Ow, ow, ow! Put that thing away!
Velvet: [i](staring at it)[/i] That's not supposed to work down here.
- Then maybe I'm not supposed to be down here.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"arrogant")
	Velvet: [i](growling, backing off)[/i] Keep telling yourself that. Everybody stays.
- Sorry. I didn't know it would do that.
	Velvet: [i](licking the burn)[/i] Sorry? To me? Oh, you won't last long.
=> END

~ asmodeus_offer
Asmodeus: There you are. I've known you for years. You just never said my name.
Asmodeus: Asmodeus. This floor is mine. People see whatever they want when they look at me.
Asmodeus: [i](glancing down at herself)[/i] So this is what you see. Interesting.
if GameState.has_crucifix
	Asmodeus: And put that little cross away. It's rude to bring a chaperone.
	- It stays.
		Asmodeus: Keep it, then. A chaperone never stopped anyone.
	- (Lower the cross.)
		Asmodeus: [i](smiling)[/i] Better. Now I can see you.
if RunStats.deaths_in_level() >= 2
	Asmodeus: {{RunStats.opening_words(RunStats.deaths_in_level())}} falls on the way to me. I felt every one.
$> Offers.present(&"lust_shortcut")
Asmodeus: [i](a lazy wave at the floor)[/i] Spend the night with me. In the morning, I'll walk you to the stairs. No more running. No more of this.
Asmodeus: Or walk. It's a long floor, darling.
- I'm tired. But no.
	$> Offers.refuse(&"lust_shortcut")
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"humble")
	Asmodeus: Tired, and still no. [i](a slow smile)[/i] I can wait, darling. I'm good at it.
- Find someone weaker. I'm not like the others.
	$> Offers.refuse(&"lust_shortcut")
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"arrogant")
	Asmodeus: [i](laughing)[/i] Not like the others. They all say that. Then the candles burn down.
- I've earned a rest. One night.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"arrogant")
	Asmodeus: “Earned.” What a lovely word. Everyone thinks they've earned me.
	$> Offers.accept(&"lust_shortcut")
- I'm so tired. Just one night.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"humble")
	Asmodeus: [i](smiling)[/i] One night. Of course. Nobody ever asks for two.
	$> Offers.accept(&"lust_shortcut")
=> END

~ asmodeus_second_offer
Asmodeus: Out of breath? Every road here ends with me, darling. You took the long one.
if RunStats.deaths_in_phase(2) >= 2
	Asmodeus: {{RunStats.opening_words(RunStats.deaths_in_phase(2))}} falls on that climb, and you keep getting up. Why?
if Moral.leans_arrogant()
	Asmodeus: You talk like you're better than this place. The others did too.
else
	Asmodeus: Still saying no. It makes the yes so much sweeter.
$> Offers.present(&"lust_shortcut")
Asmodeus: My offer stands. One night. Then the stairs.
- No. I got this far on my own.
	$> Offers.refuse(&"lust_shortcut")
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"arrogant")
	Asmodeus: On your own. That's what makes it fun to watch.
- I'm scared of what's up there. Still no.
	$> Offers.refuse(&"lust_shortcut")
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"humble")
	Asmodeus: [i](for once, she doesn't smile)[/i] Hm. That's new. It won't last.
- I can't keep climbing. Take me out.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"humble")
	Asmodeus: [i](holding out her hand)[/i] There. Was that so hard?
	$> Offers.accept(&"lust_shortcut")
- Fine. It doesn't change who I am.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"arrogant")
	Asmodeus: Of course not, darling. We'll talk in the morning.
	$> Offers.accept(&"lust_shortcut")
=> END

~ asmodeus_deaths
if RunStats.offer_zone_minutes() >= 5
	Asmodeus: {{RunStats.opening_words(RunStats.offer_zone_minutes())}} minutes on this one stretch, darling. I watched every one.
elif RunStats.offer_zone_deaths() >= 3
	Asmodeus: {{RunStats.opening_words(RunStats.offer_zone_deaths())}} times, right here. I counted. Try not to give me another.
else
	Asmodeus: This part was hard, wasn't it?
Asmodeus: Nobody dies twice down here. You just start again.
if RunStats.death_offers_made() > 1
	Asmodeus: I did ask you before. The offer still stands.
$> Offers.present(&"lust_shortcut")
Asmodeus: Say yes, and you never climb this again.
- I don't need you. I'll do it alone.
	$> Offers.refuse(&"lust_shortcut")
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"arrogant")
	Asmodeus: Alone, then. I'll watch.
- Again. I'll get up again.
	$> Offers.refuse(&"lust_shortcut")
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"humble")
	Asmodeus: Then go. I'll be right here.
- I've earned a rest.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"arrogant")
	Asmodeus: Of course you have.
	$> Offers.accept(&"lust_shortcut")
- I can't do this anymore.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"humble")
	Asmodeus: [i](softly)[/i] Shh. I know.
	$> Offers.accept(&"lust_shortcut")
=> END

~ asmodeus_gift
if Moral.has_taken(&"lust_shortcut")
	Asmodeus: You see? I keep my promises. Unlike some.
else
	Asmodeus: You walked the whole floor without me. [i](a slow smile)[/i] That was rude, darling.
Asmodeus: Every one of us gives a gift on the way out. It's how we make sure you come back.
- What gift?
- I don't want anything from you.
	Asmodeus: You haven't seen it yet.
$> Offers.present(&"charm")
Asmodeus: Charm. Look at a demon, and it stops and stares at you.
Asmodeus: It costs almost nothing. You'll just never know again if they want you, or the gift.
if GameState.has_crucifix
	Asmodeus: And your little cross won't like it. It burns near me. Keep one or the other.
- No. I'd want it too much. [if Moral.stage() < 1 and not Moral.leans_arrogant() /]
	$> Offers.refuse(&"charm")
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"humble")
	Asmodeus: [i](coldly)[/i] The offer stays open. You'll be back for it.
- Keep your tricks. I don't need them.
	$> Offers.refuse(&"charm")
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"arrogant")
	Asmodeus: Proud. How sweet. The proud ones fall the furthest.
- I can't do this alone. Give it to me.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"humble")
	$> Offers.accept(&"charm")
	Asmodeus: [i](softly)[/i] Nobody can. That's the secret.
- Give it here. I've earned it.
	$> Moral.record_tone(&"arrogant")
	$> Offers.accept(&"charm")
	Asmodeus: There. Now nobody will look away from you again.
=> END

~ stairs
Asmodeus: Run along, darling. The next floor is hungry, and they've read your file.
- My file?
	Asmodeus: [i](smiling)[/i] Every fall. Every word. Every yes and every no. Somebody keeps very good notes.
- (Climb.)
Asmodeus: Up, darling. Not down. Everyone expects down.
- (Pray.) Do You know I'm here?
	$> GameState.mark_event(&"prayed")
- (Keep climbing.)
=> END
